    "linkedin:de36b240030880a48fad6ca1": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Associate Software Engineer",
        "company": "Matacs Technologies Inc.",
        "location": "",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4479122177",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": true,
        "description": "**Company Description** \n Matacs Technologies Inc. is an innovation\\-focused company specializing in software development, robotics, and IT solutions. The organization partners with businesses to help them realize their full potential through creative and forward\\-thinking technology initiatives. By leveraging advanced tools and methodologies, Matacs aims to transform industries and challenge conventional approaches. The company is committed to delivering impactful, scalable solutions that drive long\\-term global value for its clients.\n \n\n\n\n**Role Description** \n The Associate Software Engineer will collaborate with senior engineers to design, develop, test, and maintain software applications and back\\-end web services. Day\\-to\\-day responsibilities include writing clean, efficient code, participating in code reviews, debugging and resolving technical issues, and contributing to system architecture discussions. The role also involves documenting technical specifications, working closely with cross\\-functional teams, and learning best practices in software engineering and object\\-oriented programming. This is a full\\-time, remote role based in Pakistan.\n \n\n\n\n**Qualifications** \n\n\n\n* Strong foundation in Computer Science, including core concepts such as data structures, algorithms, and software design principles.\n* Hands\\-on experience or coursework in Software Development and Programming, with proficiency in at least one modern programming language (e.g., React, Python, JavaScript).\n* Knowledge of Back\\-End Web Development, including APIs, web frameworks, and working with databases (SQL or NoSQL).\n* Understanding of Object\\-Oriented Programming (OOP) concepts and ability to apply them in practical projects.\n* Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field (or equivalent practical experience).\n* Familiarity with version control systems (e.g., Git) and collaborative development workflows.\n* Ability to analyze problems, propose solutions, and learn new technologies quickly.\n* Effective communication skills and ability to work in a team\\-oriented, on\\-site environment in Karachi.\n* Exposure to agile development methodologies and basic understanding of software testing practices is a plus.",
